  "market_context": "During a strong bullish impulse on AUDUSD 15-minute chart, price pulled back only to the shallow 0.382 Fibonacci level (0.67271) before resuming upward momentum, following an earlier Gold Zone (0.5–0.618) entry.",
  "key_observation": "After a robust upward move from ~0.6682 to ~0.6818, price retraced minimally to the 0.382 level (0.67271), not the deeper Gold Zone, indicating high momentum and trend strength.",
  "analysis_steps": [
    "Step 1: Identified a Break of Structure (BOS) at the swing low 0.6682, establishing the start of an impulse move.",
    "Step 2: Drew a Fibonacci retracement from the swing low 0.6682 (labeled '1') to the new high 0.6818 (labeled '-0.618(0.68101)').",
    "Step 3: Observed price rejecting sharply off the 0.382 retracement level (0.67271), not the deeper 0.5 or 0.618 zones, signaling strong bullish momentum.",
    "Step 4: Noted RSI behavior confirming momentum—RSI remained above 50 and did not show bearish divergence during the shallow pullback.",
    "Step 5: Set take-profit levels using Fibonacci extensions: TP1 at prior high, TP2 at -0.382, TP3 at -0.618, with potential for -1.618 in strong swing trades."
  ],
  "outcome": null,
  "lessons": "Strong momentum moves often produce shallow retracements (e.g., 0.382 instead of Gold Zone); traders should adjust entry expectations and avoid waiting for deeper pullbacks when RSI and structure confirm trend strength.",
